{{- /*
  The page the platform's own hosts get while the platform is down: api,
  identity, mcp, os and vscode under the domain. Not the bare domain itself,
  which is the cluster owner's main website and gets the neutral page.
  errorpages.go says why.

  Everything is inline because nothing else may be reachable while this page
  is up: one stylesheet, the mark in the markup, the wordmark face as a data:
  URI inside that stylesheet, no script, no image. The Content-Security-Policy
  the server sends allows this one stylesheet by hash, and a data: font, and
  nothing else.
*/ -}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" content="#f7f7f5">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" content="#07090a">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{.Message}}">
<style>
/*
  THE PALETTE IS THE BRAND'S, WRITTEN OUT. brand/tokens.css is the one source,
  but a page that may fetch nothing cannot import it, so these six values are
  copied from it and errorpages_test.go fails the build when they drift. They
  are written as a plain light set plus a dark override rather than as the
  tokens' light-dark(): a browser that does not know light-dark() would drop
  every colour, and this is the page that has to render for everybody.
*/
:root {
  --bg: #f7f7f5;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --fg: #191d1a;
  --muted: #5b615c;
  --line: #e5e6e2;
  --accent: #047d5a;
  color-scheme: light dark;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #07090a;
    --surface: #0b1110;
    --fg: #e8e6dd;
    --muted: #9ca395;
    --line: #18231e;
    --accent: #5ccda7;
  }
}

*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

/*
  The wordmark face, Squada One, carried inline: nothing here can be fetched,
  and the identity pages set their wordmark in this face, so a page that is to
  look like the platform carries it. It is the brand's own latin file, 5,632
  bytes, and errorpages_test.go fails the build when the copy drifts from
  brand/fonts. It is the only font in the page: the body text takes the
  system face, so a machine without Inter reads it in its own. The block
  period is the right one for inline data, where there is nothing to wait for
  and a flash of the wrong face on the one word that names the product would
  be the only thing to see.
*/
@font-face {
  font-family: "Squada One";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: block;
  src: url("data:font/woff2;base64,{{.Wordmark}}") format("woff2");
}

/* The brand's body stack, faces first; only the system faces can be reached from here. */
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  min-height: 100vh;
  min-height: 100dvh;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: "InterVariable", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* A border, not a shadow, and the brand's radius: the same card the sign-in page is. */
main {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 26rem;
  padding: 2.75rem 2rem 2.5rem;
  text-align: center;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 0.625rem;
}

.brand {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
}
.mark {
  display: block;
  width: 2.5rem;
  height: 2.5rem;
  color: var(--accent);
}
.mark svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
/* The face has the one weight, which is what identity's .brand-name sets it at. */
.name {
  font-family: "Squada One", "InterVariable", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, sans-serif;
  font-size: 2rem;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

h1 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.35;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
p {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* A slow breath on the mark: a thing that is running, saying so. Held still for anyone who asks. */
@keyframes breathe { 50% { opacity: 0.55; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .mark { animation: breathe 4s ease-in-out infinite; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<div class="brand">
<span class="mark">{{.Mark}}</span>
<span class="name">MemQL</span>
</div>
<h1>{{.Heading}}</h1>
<p>{{.Detail}}</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
